    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JOB 32:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because Job was convinced of his own innocence, the three men gave up trying to answer him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JOB.32.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JOB.32.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JOB 32:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But a bystander named Elihu could not control his anger any longer, because Job was justifying himself and blaming God. (Elihu was the son of Barakel, a descendant of Buz, and belonged to the clan of Ram.) ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JOB.32.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JOB.32.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JOB 32:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He was also angry with Job's three friends. They could find no way to answer Job, and this made it appear that God was in the wrong. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JOB.32.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JOB.32.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JOB 32:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because Elihu was the youngest one there, he had waited until everyone finished speaking. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JOB.32.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JOB.32.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JOB 32:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When he saw that the three men could not answer Job, he was angry ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JOB.32.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JOB.32.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JOB 32:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and began to speak.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JOB.32.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JOB.32.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
